used for PLONK-based circuits or other PIOPs.\n\nFor questions or discussions, please use the Telegram group, t.me/plonky3.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nJoin Us in Advancing Zero-Knowledge Proofs (https://blog.polyhedra.network/join-us-in-advancing-zero-knowledge-proofs/)\nciteturn6search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.4 years ago; Crawled: 4 months ago; In 2019, the Polyhedra Network co-founders embarked on a mission to explore the potential of zero-knowledge proofs. ... Libra: Succinct Zero-Knowledge Proofs with Optimal Prover Computation ... Transparent Polynomial Delegation and Its Applications to Zero Knowledge Proof\n# Join Us in Advancing Zero-Knowledge Proofs\n\nJun 12, 2024\n\n## Our Journey of Innovation\n\nInnovation is our spirit. In 2019, the Polyhedra Network co-founders embarked on a mission to explore the potential of zero-knowledge proofs. Our pioneering work, including papers such as “Libra,” “Orion,” “zkBridge,” and “Pianist,” marked the beginning of an exciting journey. Our dedication to research has led to significant advancements in zero-knowledge technology, consistently pushing the boundaries of what’s possible in the field.\n\nCheck out our progress: https://polyhedra.medium.com/why-polyhedra-network-zk-67420617602c\n\nLibra: Succinct Zero-Knowledge Proofs with Optimal Prover Computation\nhttps://eprint.iacr.org/2019/317.pdf\n\nTransparent Polynomial Delegation and Its Applications to Zero Knowledge Proof\nhttps://eprint.iacr.org/2019/1482.pdf\n\nOrion: Zero Knowledge Proof with Linear Prover Time\nhttps://eprint.iacr.org/2022/1010.pdf\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLightZK: An Efficient GPU Acceleration Framework for Large-Scale Zero-Knowledge Proofs - 科研通 (https://www.ablesci.com/assist/detail?id=58MwrQ)\nciteturn6search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: last week; Crawled: last week; 标题  | Image: Association for Computing Machinery (AC